WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/settings/pages/PrivacyPage.tsx — the first-class `/account/privacy` page promoted out of
  Settings. It is a THIN shell: `PageContainer(title=t('account.privacy.title','Privacy'),
  subtitle=t('account.privacy.subtitle', 'Manage browser-local data: recently viewed pages and cookies /
  analytics consent.'), copyLink)` wrapping `<PrivacySection/>` 1:1. PageContainer renders an <h1> title, a
  muted <p> subtitle, and (copyLink) a <CopyLinkButton> (i18n keys common.copyLink.action/copied/label/success;
  link→check glyph swap, copies window.location.href). All privacy state (recent-pages LRU, tri-state cookie
  consent, the destructive clear ConfirmDialog + its silence opt-in, the toast) lives inside PrivacySection.
  No API data sources at the page tier (renders from local state). Charts/maps: none.

